## eBay OAuth publish

- Server: `server/ebay-api.mjs` → `/api/ebay/*` (`status`, `oauth/*`, `policies`, `publish`, `revise`).
- `POST /api/ebay/publish` accepts `dry_run: true` (validate only, no Inventory writes).
- `POST /api/ebay/revise` → `bulk_update_price_quantity` (+ optional withdraw at qty 0).
- Env: `EBAY_CLIENT_ID`, `EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET`, `EBAY_RU_NAME`, optional `EBAY_ENV=sandbox`.
- Catalog defaults: dry-run ON, daily cap + ramp, kill switch. Live requires explicit UI confirm.

## Catalog flow

1. Import CSV/JSON (column aliases in `csvImport.js`)
2. Enrich & price → `PENDING_REVIEW` or `NEEDS_ATTENTION`
3. Human approve → `APPROVED`
4. Publish batch (respects daily cap / kill switch / dry-run)
5. Stock/price sync for `LISTED` items via revise

## Orders & customer service (ops)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `lib/listingengine/ops/orders.js` | Sync Fulfillment orders, mark supplier-ordered, upload tracking |
| `lib/listingengine/ops/customerService.js` | Inquiry sync / manual cases / LLM draft / approve-before-send |
| `OrdersPanel.jsx` / `CsInboxPanel.jsx` | UI under Katalog → Bestellungen / Kundenservice |

- `GET /api/ebay/orders`, `POST /api/ebay/orders/:id/ship` (createShippingFulfillment)
- `GET /api/ebay/inquiries`, `POST /api/ebay/inquiries/:id/reply` (Post-Order; human_approved required)
- CS without inquiry ID: draft + copy to clipboard for Seller Hub
- Never invent tracking/refunds in drafts; dry-run respects catalog setting

## Do not

- Put Anthropic or eBay secrets in `VITE_*`.
- Let AI rewrite locked legal modules.
- Register Listing Engine as a suite `TabBar` tab without product decision.
- Publish when compliance is blocked or the listing is not human-approved.
- Invent SEO title attributes not present in product data.
- Browser-bot or scrape retail marketplaces for supplier data.
